{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0953"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c080): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c080.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0953"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/olympics","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__olympics.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",882],["+","The cancellations also explain a surprisingly short German record. Of all the Games awarded to Germany, only 3 were actually held between 1900 and 2014: the Winter Games at Garmisch-Partenkirchen in February 1936, the Summer Games in Berlin in August 1936 and the Summer Games in Munich in 1972. Berlin 1916 and Garmisch-Partenkirchen 1940 exist only in the record books of what might have been.\n\n"],["=",87]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",824],["+","Die Absagen erklären auch eine überraschend kurze deutsche Bilanz. Von allen an Deutschland vergebenen Spielen fanden zwischen 1900 und 2014 nur 3 tatsächlich statt: die Winterspiele in Garmisch-Partenkirchen im Februar 1936, die Sommerspiele in Berlin im August 1936 und die Sommerspiele in München 1972. Berlin 1916 und Garmisch-Partenkirchen 1940 existieren nur in den Annalen dessen, was hätte sein können.\n\n"],["=",85]]}]},
